<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="JirAI: Support" id="JirAI-Reference-and-Support">

    <primary-label ref="jirai"/>

    <link-summary>Report a problem with JirAI, request a feature, contact the vendor and read the legal terms.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Report a problem, request a feature, contact the vendor and read the legal terms.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>Get help with JirAI for Jira Cloud in JetBrains IDEs: report bugs and feature requests, contact the vendor by e-mail, and read the terms and privacy policy.</web-summary>

    <p>Use the options below to get help with JirAI or to suggest an improvement.</p>

    <include from="common-support.topic" element-id="support-content"/>

    <chapter title="What to include in a report" id="feature-requests">
        <list>
            <li><p>Your IDE name and version, from <ui-path>Help | About</ui-path>.</p></li>
            <li><p>The JirAI version, from <ui-path>Settings | Plugins</ui-path>.</p></li>
            <li><p>Whether you use Remote Development.</p></li>
            <li><p>The steps that lead to the problem, and what you expected instead.</p></li>
            <li><p>The relevant part of the IDE log: <ui-path>Help | Show Log in Finder</ui-path> on macOS, or <ui-path>Help | Show Log in Explorer</ui-path> on Windows.</p></li>
        </list>
        <p>Never include your API token.</p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Licensing questions" id="contact">
        <p>For questions about licenses, write to <a href="mailto:jgafner@dorkag.com">jgafner@dorkag.com</a>.</p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Terms and privacy" id="legal">
        <list>
            <li><p>JirAI is licensed under the <a href="terms-of-service.topic">Terms of Service</a>.</p></li>
            <li><p>The <a href="privacy-policy.topic">Privacy Policy</a> describes what data the DORKAG plugins handle.</p></li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

